==English==

===Etymology===
First attested during the 19th century, in the US, as a fanciful alteration of the noun {{m|en|lick}} “a very fast sprint”, and the verb {{m|en|split}}. The forms {{m|en|lickety-cut}} and {{m|en|licketie}} are similarly attested.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-lickety-split.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[quickly|Quickly]]; as [[fast]] as possible; in short order.
#: ''At the sound of the starting gun, they were off and running '''lickety-split'''.''
#: ''I need tea right now, '''lickety-split'''.''
#* {{seeCites|en|lickety}}

